{
  "id": "28245_kirikawaru",
  "headword": "{切|き}り{替|か}わる",
  "reading": "きりかわる",
  "romaji": "kirikawaru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to switch over; to change over; to be switched",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to switch over; to change over (to a new state or mode)",
      "explanation": "For a system, display, signal, or mode to change from one state to another. The intransitive counterpart of {切|き}り{替|か}える; the change happens by itself or automatically rather than being done to an object."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28245_kirikawaru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{画面|がめん}が{切|き}り{替|か}わった。",
      "english": "The screen switched over.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28245_kirikawaru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{信号|しんごう}が{青|あお}に{切|き}り{替|か}わる。",
      "english": "The traffic light changes to green.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28245_kirikawaru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{四月|しがつ}になると{自動的|じどうてき}に{新|あたら}しい{料金|りょうきん}プランに{切|き}り{替|か}わる。",
      "english": "When April comes, it automatically switches over to the new rate plan.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}).\n- Pair: {切|き}り{替|か}える (transitive — to switch something over).\n- Pattern: Xが(Yに){切|き}り{替|か}わる\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {画面|がめん}が{切|き}り{替|か}わる: the screen changes\n- {自動|じどう}で{切|き}り{替|か}わる: switches automatically\n- {表示|ひょうじ}が{切|き}り{替|か}わる: the display changes over",
